  "method": [
    "20-second full-frame DIRTYFB loop at 60 requested updates/s, with a one-second settle before and after; function profiling and usbmon enabled. These are diagnostic traced runs, not clean CPU benchmarks.",
    "Throughput uses successful whole-frame bulk completions from the longest contiguous run matching the expected wire frame size, excluding two seconds at each end. Units are decimal MB/s.",
    "Sampled variant adds one status-consumption run per second to the existing interrupt worker, and logs its already-read status. No competing raw status reader or permanent production interface is added.",
    "edid-off additionally clears only bit 30 in each outgoing 0x8020 register write, including initialization and every I2C command. All other bits and the bridge driver are unchanged.",
    "Loaded case runs a busy shell loop alongside the KMS workload on the sole guest vCPU. No competing physical USB traffic was generated.",
    "Controller frame-counter rate is computed over the same steady-state window. It does not establish that distinct complete images reached the HDMI sink.",
    "Bulk completion errno -2 is ENOENT from deliberate modeset/restore URB cancellation; these are outside the selected steady-state completion run.",
    "Source hashes describe final files; the only edit after module builds was a kernel-doc sentence explaining the frame-sync bit."
  ],
