  "conclusions": [
    "Native formats and atomic smoke checks passed with ordered programming; physical register traces show separate watermark-reset and format-selection writes.",
    "1080p completed USB frame rate is about 30/s for both wire depths while the controller counter advances about 60/s. Neither RGB565 nor clearing bit 30 resolved it in this setup.",
    "All sampled steady-state status words retain LBUF overflow, with no sampled underflow. Existing acknowledgment writes observed bits 8/9, whereas the manual specifies writing bit 31 and separately documents 0x8004 bit 12. Sticky status cannot establish an overflow event rate.",
    "Keep current detection and bandwidth policy. No pacing algorithm is justified from this limited transport-only test."
  ],
  "remaining_tests": [
    "Use a 1080p-capable display or HDMI capture to assess actual distinct frames and glitches; repeat with a dedicated controller or physical host to separate passthrough effects.",
    "Validate LBUF clear semantics and recovery before treating sampled flags as event counters.",
    "Measure sustained bandwidth and scanline margin under real competing USB traffic; these tests did not achieve the 373.248 MB/s required for full 1080p60 RGB888 delivery.",
    "Repeat longer, alternating A/B trials and HPD tests before changing detection policy or introducing pacing."
  ]
